<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50612" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰότης</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ητος</span>, ἡ</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>will, desire</i>, 
				Ep.
			and Lyr. almost always in dat., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῶν ἰότητι</span>
			<i>by the will</i> of the gods, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				19.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				7.214
			</span></i>,al., cf.<i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				13
			</span></i>A; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μητρὸς ἐμῆς ἰότητι</span>
			<i>at</i> her <i>will</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				18.396
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακῆς ἰ. γυναικός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.384
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μνηστήρων ἰ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				18.234
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλήλων ἰ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.874
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναιδήτῳ ἰ</span>. with
			shameless <i>will</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.360
			</span></i>: acc. only in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				15.41
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι᾽ ἐμὴν ἰ</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> once in Trag., <i>for the sake of</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰότατι γάμων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					558
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).—<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> explains it by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βουλήσει, αἰτία,
				ὀργῇ, χάριτι</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
